# PrimeNG residual theme & token maintenance (PNO-1323)

Use this alongside `design-system-protection.mdc` and `tasks/ui-technical-cleanup/cleanup_primeng-overrides.plan.md`.

## Deliberate state (not bugs to “fix” in passing)

1. **Tailwind hex duplication** — **Resolved in PNO-1369.** Tailwind 4 supports `var()` natively with opacity modifiers. The JS-based `tailwind.config.js` was replaced by a CSS-native `@theme` block in `src/tailwind.css`. Color hex values are still present in both `unops-design-tokens.css` and `tailwind.css @theme`, but the duplication is no longer a functional limitation. When updating a UNOPS color, update both files.

2. **`unops.preset.ts` primary scale** — A **literal hex** (e.g. `#0092d1` around the primary palette definition) is **structural** to how PrimeNG Aura/preset APIs express color scales. It is not the same problem as Tailwind duplication; changing it requires a deliberate palette decision, not a drive-by cleanup.

3. **`primeng-unops-theme.scss` (~1.5k lines)** — **Layer 3**: global hooks the **preset cannot express**. After the `!important` purge, remaining rules should shrink over time; **do not** assume the file should be deleted wholesale.

## Ongoing actions (reviewer agreement)

- When **PrimeNG adds preset/design tokens** that cover a rule in `primeng-unops-theme.scss`, **remove or narrow** that rule and prefer preset/tokens.
- When **refactoring a component**, check whether **global hooks** in `primeng-unops-theme.scss` that targeted old markup still apply; **delete obsolete** selectors/blocks.
- **Do not add** new large `.p-*` override blocks in feature SCSS; **residual global** styling belongs in the theme file only when necessary, and the **PR template** “Design system & PrimeNG” checklist is the gate.

## Branch / deploy note

Large styling cleanup (e.g. “Remove `!important`” batch) may land on **`feature/PNO-1323-ui-technical-cleanup`** or **`development`** first. **`dev-deploy`** must be **merged/rebased** from that line of history when ready to ship those changes — verify the latest commit on the source branch rather than relying on a fixed SHA in this rule.

## QA exception

Per `qa-write-boundaries.mdc`, QA-only folders are unchanged; this rule governs **production** ClientApp styling maintenance.
